[size=4][color=#F5A623][b]Modlist Compare[/b][/color][/size]

[b]An MO2 plugin for comparing modlists - see what another list has that yours doesn't, side by side, without leaving Mod Organizer 2.[/b]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Description[/b][/color][/size]
Adds a [b]Modlist Compare[/b] submenu to MO2's Tools menu with two entries: one exports the active profile's modlist to JSON, and one generates reports comparing any two lists - an exported JSON file, your current profile, or one of each. The reports are the same ones the [url=https://github.com/imightbemeteor/meteoric-modlist-tools]meteoric-modlist-tools[/url] command-line tools produce, from the same code, with the same file naming, so plugin output and CLI output are interchangeable.

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Installation Instructions[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab[/*]
[*]Unzip it into your MO2 installation's [b]plugins/[/b] folder - the archive already contains the [b]modlist_compare/[/b] folder, so you should end up with [b]plugins/modlist_compare/[/b][/*]
[*]Restart MO2 - [b]Tools > Modlist Compare[/b] appears in the toolbar's tools menu[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Main Features[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Coverage report[/b] - What a target list is missing or behind on compared to a source list, with per-mod states and a percent-covered badge (HTML)[/*]
[*][b]Diff report[/b] - Both lists' full ordering side by side, colour-coded, including moves (HTML)[/*]
[*][b]Changelog[/b] - Added, removed, and updated mods between two versions of a list (markdown)[/*]
[*][b]Live profile support[/b] - Compare against your current profile directly, no export step needed[/*]
[*][b]Smart matching[/b] - Mods are matched across lists by Nexus IDs, plugin files, and names, so renames and merges are handled[/*]
[*][b]GitHub Action[/b] - Modlist repos can generate and publish these reports automatically on every release (see below)[/*]
[*][b]Responsive UI[/b] - Generation runs behind a progress dialog with live percent and cancel; MO2 stays responsive, not frozen[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]How to Use[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Export a list[/b] - Tools, Modlist Compare, Export Modlist to JSON saves the active profile[/*]
[*][b]Open Generate Reports[/b] - Pick List 1 (source/old) and List 2 (target/new): a JSON file or the current profile, with at least one side a file[/*]
[*][b]Choose reports[/b] - Any combination of Coverage, Diff, and Changelog, plus a destination folder[/*]
[*][b]Generate[/b] - Reports are written to the destination; Open Folder takes you straight there[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]For Modlist Maintainers: GitHub Action[/b][/color][/size]
If your list lives in a GitHub repo (Wabbajack lists, for example), the same reports can be generated for you on every release. Export your list with this plugin, commit the JSON to a [b]lists/[/b] folder in your repo, and a GitHub Action opens a pull request with the changelog, diff, and coverage reports comparing it against the previous version, plus a CHANGELOG.md entry skeleton for you to fill in. Enable GitHub Pages and the HTML reports are served straight from the repo.
[list]
[*]Instructions and the copy-paste workflow: [url=https://github.com/imightbemeteor/meteoric-modlist-tools#github-action]meteoric-modlist-tools#github-action[/url][/*]
[*]Live example - Nordic Souls PBR: [url=https://skrubbyskrubinashrub.github.io/nordic-souls-PBR/changelog/v1.5.0/diff.html]diff[/url] | [url=https://skrubbyskrubinashrub.github.io/nordic-souls-PBR/changelog/v1.5.0/coverage.html]coverage[/url] | [url=https://github.com/SkrubbySkrubInAShrub/nordic-souls-PBR/blob/main/changelog/v1.5.0/changelog.md]changelog[/url][/*]
[*]It compares the two newest exports, so your first PR arrives with your [i]second[/i] release - a single JSON produces nothing[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Requirements[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Mod Organizer 2 [b]2.5.0 or newer[/b] (the PyQt6-based Python runtime)[/*]
[*]Nothing else - no third-party Python packages[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Known Limitations[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]The coverage ignore list is read but not edited from the plugin; use the CLI's serve mode or a text editor to change it[/*]
[*]Report generation vendors its modules under plain names (modlist_utils and friends); another Python plugin shipping a same-named top-level module could collide - none known[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][color=#F5A623][b]Source[/b][/color][/size]
The plugin is open source - the code lives in the [url=https://github.com/imightbemeteor/meteoric-modlist-tools/tree/main/mo2-plugins/modlist_compare]mo2-plugins/modlist_compare[/url] folder of the meteoric-modlist-tools repository, alongside the command-line tools that share its report generators.

